cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the released artefacts, please cite the paper below."
title: "Quantile-Shrink: Distribution-Free Per-Cube Threshold Calibration for 3D Point Cloud Change Detection"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Amanzunge/quantile-shrink-3dcd"
url: "https://github.com/Amanzunge/quantile-shrink-3dcd"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen calibration outputs and result tables for a systematic study of
  decision-threshold calibration in cube-tiled 3D point cloud change detection:
  seven calibration rules, six detection models and four datasets under one frozen
  protocol, plus quantile-shrink, a per-cube threshold built from the conformal-rank
  quantile of each cube's predicted no-change scores and shrunk toward the
  scene-level quantile with an empirical-Bayes weight.
